From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] rockchip: rk3399: Rigol DHO800/DHO900 and MHO900, the
 NovaOS U-Boot proper

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

U-Boot proper only, for the Rigol oscilloscopes' RK3399 (LPDDR4, the boot
medium an SD card on sdmmc, console UART2 at 115200), one defconfig per family
(nova-dho900-rk3399_defconfig, nova-mho900-rk3399_defconfig: the same board,
each with its own control DT and root compatible) and two flavors merged over
it from board/rigol/nova_rk3399/:

  nova-kexec-test.config  a running NovaOS kexecs u-boot.bin with the RK3399
                          watchdog counting; `nova kexec-test` checks that what
                          kexec handed over is what was loaded (the initrd, the
                          FDT, its own code, against sizes and crc32s on the
                          kexec command line, and the Ethernet MAC's receive
                          ring as the kernel left it), reports the CPU and card
                          clocks, times the card and an LZ4 decompression,
                          writes the results into the ramoops pmsg zone, and
                          `nova reset` resets the SoC.
  nova-chainload.config   Rigol's stock U-Boot 2014.10 loads u-boot.bin from
                          `recovery` as the kernel of an ANDROID! image (raw, at
                          0x280000, EL2, x0 = its FDT; BL31 and OP-TEE stay
                          resident); `nova boot` boots NovaOS from the LZ4 FIT
                          appended to that image, with the command line the
                          stock U-Boot built. It keeps a ladder of attempts
                          (nova_chain.c): the committed image, a new one on
                          trial from a slot in `backup` (booted through its own
                          U-Boot), the committed image's copy, then the stock
                          firmware. The RK3399 watchdog is armed in
                          board_early_init_f and never fed, and a record in
                          PMUGRF OS_REG1 counts the attempts across resets.
                          Kexec'd from a running NovaOS instead (the watchdog
                          already counting at entry, no slot handed over), it
                          boots the FIT passed as the kexec initrd after timing
                          the same card reads, keeps the GIC's LPI tables for
                          the next kernel (/memreserve/), leaves the record in
                          OS_REG1 alone, and on any failure resets with no
                          reboot flag.

Both flavors quiet U-Boot only (SILENT_U_BOOT_ONLY: silent=1 alone makes bootm
rewrite the kernel's console= as console=ttynull), and the chainload gives the
FDT bootm shrinks room again for /bootstage (ft_board_setup_ex, SYS_FDT_PAD).

Neither flavor has a watchdog driver, MMC writes, a saved environment, the
boot-mode register (ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG=0: no download-key check, so no
write of BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD), ADC, PMIC/regulator/PWM/SPI/PCI/USB/video
drivers, or a reprogrammed PLL (the control DT drops the CRUs' assigned
clocks). Both build lib/ for speed (CC_OPTIMIZE_LIBS_FOR_SPEED: the LZ4 decoder
and crc32 of a 27 MB kernel). The DRAM banks lose the stock OP-TEE region, as the /memory node the
stock U-Boot passes to the kernel does. Build only `make u-boot.bin`: no
TPL/SPL, DRAM and BL31 are the stock loaders'.

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
